hangelog">v<!-- -->3.4.0</a></div></aside><main class="documentation-sidebar__content"><h1 class="bold" id="rule-of-3-cs"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="rule-of-3-cs#rule-of-3-cs">Rule of 3 Cs</a></h1>
<h2 class="bold" id="-1-containers"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="rule-of-3-cs#-1-containers">№ 1: Containers</a></h2>
<p>Containers are elements that contain other elements. Typical examples of these
are cards, modals, etc.</p>
<p>**Use padding on all sides for the container&#x27;s content **- like matte in
framed photos (common examples could be Cards or Alerts).</p>
<p><strong>Remove margin-bottom of the bottom-most element in the container stack</strong>. It
would only add up to the padding property of the container. <strong>We want to keep
spacing predictable</strong> so we want to prevent adding-up like that.</p>
